#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Measure the TF2 Soldier bot's blast jump on ss_ai_tf_jump (plan_bots_teams_tf2_part_g G0, G.5).

  tools/ai-tf-jump measure [--seconds 240] [--config debug] [--out FILE.json] [--keep] [--walk-health 110]
  tools/ai-tf-jump read FILE.json      an earlier run's numbers again, from its kept track
  tools/ai-tf-jump record [--seconds 300] [--config debug] [--keep] [--rec FILE.airec]
  tools/ai-tf-jump sim [--config debug|release]   the simulator against the recording: its gaps and its speed
  tools/ai-tf-jump links [--tries 10] [--others] [--reload] [--think-log] [--config debug] [--out FILE.json] [--keep]
  tools/ai-tf-jump trust --db FILE.db [--tries 10] [--config debug] [--out FILE.json]
  tools/ai-tf-jump course [--runs 5] [--reload] [--db FILE.db] [--config debug] [--out FILE.json] [--think-log] [--map ss_ai_tf_double|ss_ai_tf_wall|ss_ai_tf_ends]
  tools/ai-tf-jump --self-test

Starts a headless tf2 game on the map (tools/ai-scenario's Game: its own
instance, temp dir, dev-API directory and port), adds one red Soldier, and
runs two arms of --seconds each with the bot's brain deciding:

  jump   its health held at 200 (`ai_aim_tough`), so it may rocket jump
  walk   its health held at --walk-health (110): a jump must leave the bot 90
         (TFDecider.RocketJumpHealthFloor) after its blast and no blast costs
         under 20, so it makes none; and it is over the 40 % at which a bot
         leaves for a health pack: the same walk, no jump. (Before G5c the floor
         was on the health before the jump and this arm was held at 85.)

The bot has nobody to fight, so it plays capture the flag alone, round and
round: east along the run for the blue flag, west along it carrying, east
under the low lane's slab to its capture zone, and west under the slab with
nothing in its hands. A carrier never jumps, so each arm holds its own walk
beside it. Its place is read from the game (`/ai/world`, about ten times a
second, each sample stamped with the server's tick), and every time it
crosses a lane's middle stretch (x 500 to 1700, 1,200 u) without leaving the
lane, that is one traverse of that lane and direction:

  n        traverses
  seconds  the median time over the stretch, by server ticks
  speed    1,200 u over that, u/s
  peak     the highest the bot's feet rose over the floor in a traverse, u
  hops     times in a traverse it left the floor by more than 24 u

and the applier's count of ability sequences begun in the arm
(`ai.apply.ability.sequences`). A round's restart puts the bot back on its
spawn: a step faster than 1,500 u/s is that, and drops the traverse it was in.
Each flight is listed too: a time off the floor that rose past half the lowest
apex of the plans the game holds (`/ai/jumps`, as the game itself tells a
flight from a hop), or past 200 u for a game that serves none:

  air      seconds off the floor
  along    how far it went over the floor in that time, u (a walk covers 240 u a second)
  walked   the same time at the bot's own walking speed, u

Since G5c the jump is a program that flies a planned recipe, and the game
counts each one (`/ai/jumps`, the TF2 binding's route). Per arm, from that:

  jumps    begun, and how each ended: landed (near the plan's touch, short of
           it, elsewhere), called off (the view late, astray), fizzled, died,
           timed out
  slab     jumps whose takeoff was under the low lane's slab: must be 0
  flown    each landed jump: seconds in the air, ground covered from its
           takeoff, how far past the plan's takeoff it launched, how far from
           the plan's touch it came down, how high it rose, and how many of
           them stood for a late view and for how long
  off      each jump that did not land: how it ended, after how long, where
           against its plan's takeoff, and how long it had stood
  gap      the differential: how far the game's landing is from where the
           simulator comes down flying the same recipe from the same launch
           state (the worker flies it after each jump), median and worst
  book     stretches asked, planned and refused by reason, and what the
           worker spent (simulated flights, floods of the graph, CPU)

A game built before G5c serves no `/ai/jumps`; those parts are then empty.

`record` plays the jump arm alone with the AI session recorded (`ai_record`),
and writes what the blast-jump simulator's differential facts replay
(BlastJumpDifferentialTests, G.5 step 3):

  src/ai/tests/recordings/ss_ai_tf_jump.airec   the bot's usercmds and frames (where it stood and moved each
                                                tick) around each flight: 100 ticks before it left the floor
                                                to 34 after it came back; the rest of the session is cut
  src/ai/tests/recordings/ss_ai_tf_jump.json    the map source's sha256, the game's commit, the flights
                                                this tool saw, the bot's slot, what was cut and the counters

With --rec FILE.airec (lane G7b) the recording and its .json go there instead, the .json with
the game's jumps (`/ai/jumps`, each with its gap to the simulator's flight): for a test build's
flights, which the committed recording must never hold.

`links` (lane G5c-2b) sends the Soldier, by its brain (`ai_tf_errand`, which gives
its tree a place to go), to the top of the 250 u ledge, a place only a blast link
reaches, --tries times (10), each from the same spot on the floor
(`LINK_START`), its health held at 200. A try is the brain's: the route takes the
link, the follower leads the bot to the link's start, the tree begins the jump and
the program flies the link's recipe. Per try, by server ticks: whether the bot got
there (on the ledge's floor, within `ARRIVE_FLAT` of the place), how long it took,
the jumps it began and how each ended, whether it got there by a link (a landed
jump whose plan is a link's, `/ai/jumps` `plan` at `LINK_ARGUMENT_BASE` or over),
and the landing's gap to the simulator's flight of the same recipe from the same
launch (`gap`) and to the link's own touch (`off_plan`). A jump the game ended as
`Moved` (a round's restart put the bot on its spawn in mid-flight, lane G5e) is no
landing. Fizzles with a blast
felt one or two commands after the trigger are counted apart (the mod's rocket on
a teammate: none here, there is one bot). Then, with --others, each other landing
of a link with no walk to it once; with --reload, the level is loaded again in
the same process (`changelevel`), the links come from the cache, and --tries more.
With --out FILE.json the run's console lines go beside it (FILE.console.log).
The game's own link counters (`ai.jump.link.*`) are printed with the summary.

`trust` (lane G5e) proves that a link's tries reach the experience store and that a
link the tries say fails is left out. The game runs with a private store (`--db`, a
file that must not exist yet: the rows are this run's). The ledge is tried --tries
times (phase A), the round is restarted (`mp_restartgame 1`: the round's end flushes
the tries, its start loads the snapshot again), the tool waits for the routes the
new snapshot makes (`/ai/experience` routes.builds) and the ledge is tried --tries
times more (phase B). It prints each phase's tries as `links` does, the links the
snapshot left out (`/ai/experience` routes.shut), whether phase B began any of them
(it must not), and, after the game, the store's `link` rows read from the file
(class, bins, tries, successes, mean seconds and health). On a normal build every
link lands and none is left out; to see one left out, a test build spoils a link's
recipe (the run's evidence says how).

`course` (lane G7a) runs the jump course, ss_ai_tf_course (TFAiTestMaps.Course: seven
stages S0..S6 over a pit, each reached from the one before only by a blast jump, a
control point on each after the first, a cabinet in a bay off each, a reset teleport under
each jump). One red Soldier is added and sent nowhere: no errand, its health not held, its
own tree's Course branch takes it. Each of --runs runs (5) starts with `mp_restartgame 1`
(the course's points go back to nobody's, the bot to its spawn on S0) and watches the bot,
by server ticks, until it stands on the last stage or RUN_TICKS go by. Per run, per stage:
the tick it first stood on the stage's top (from the run's start); per jump (J1..J6, the
level's links by their takeoff and landing stages): the tries begun (`/ai/jumps` `last`,
a plan at LINK_ARGUMENT_BASE or over) and how each ended, the falls (a Reset end, or the bot's
feet more than FALL_UNITS under the stage it took off from; a Moved end, a round's restart
catching the bot in a jump, is counted apart), and the bot's
health as it left the stage's top (the dev API's `/entity`); the times it stood in a
stage's cabinet bay; the decides it ran another branch than Course before the end. With
--reload, the level is loaded again in the same process (`changelevel`, links from the
cache) and --runs more. With --db FILE.db (a new file) the game keeps a private store and
its `link` rows are printed after. A run finishes when the bot stands on S6; the tool
fails unless 4 of 5 (80 %) of the runs before the reload and after it finish. With
--map ss_ai_tf_double (lane G7b) the course is the second rocket's: S0..S2, S2 reached by
a link with a second rocket in the air; each such jump is printed with when its second
trigger was pressed, its gap to the simulator and its plan's health, and each jump's
health as the bot arrived on the next stage beside its health at takeoff. With --map
ss_ai_tf_wall (lane G7c) it is the wall jump's: the same stages, S2 reached by a link whose
second rocket is fired at a wall beside the way (no beam under it).
With --map ss_ai_tf_ends (lane Ge) the course is a hub and several courses whose ends are
capture areas naming no point (TFAiTestMaps.Ends, as jump_academy2_rc9a's are): the ends
reached are the game's, read from `/ai/course` (the ends the bot stood in this life); a run
starts once the restart's respawn has made the bot forget them (`reached` empty) and is
finished when the route says every end is reached; per end, the tick it was reached and the
link tries begun meanwhile by how they ended.

`sim` runs the simulator's facts (BlastJumpDifferentialTests and
BlastJumpSpeedTests) and prints the numbers they write under
bin/<config>/ai-jump/: each recorded flight flown again from its takeoff
state, the gap in apex, air time and landing place (medians and the worst),
and how many flights a second one core simulates. The debug build is
`make ai-test`'s; `--config release` builds and runs the same facts optimised
(`dotnet test -c Release`), which is the speed a played server has, and needs
the map built for it (`make map MAP=ss_ai_tf_jump CONFIG=release`). No game
is started. A report the facts did not write is a failure.

The map is per-tree build output: `make map MAP=ss_ai_tf_jump` first; a
missing map is a failure.
"""
import argparse
import hashlib
import importlib.machinery
import importlib.util
import json
import os
import re
import statistics
import struct
import subprocess
import sys
import time

ROOT = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__)))
MAP = "ss_ai_tf_jump"

# TFAiTestMaps' numbers: the floor's top, the lanes across the room, the stretch timed.
FLOOR_Z = 16.0
LANES = {"run": (16.0, 448.0), "low": (464.0, 800.0)}
STRETCH = (500.0, 1700.0)
HOP_UNITS = 24.0
FLIGHT_UNITS = 200.0
TELEPORT_SPEED = 1500.0
WALK_SPEED = 240.0

_loader = importlib.machinery.SourceFileLoader("ai_scenario", os.path.join(ROOT, "tools", "ai-scenario"))
_spec = importlib.util.spec_from_loader("ai_scenario", _loader)
ai_scenario = importlib.util.module_from_spec(_spec)
_loader.exec_module(ai_scenario)


def lane_of(y):
    """The lane a y lies in, or None. PURE."""
    for name, (lo, hi) in LANES.items():
        if lo <= y <= hi:
            return name
    return None


def crossing_tick(a, b, x):
    """The tick at which the walk from sample a to sample b passes x, by a
    straight line between them. Samples are (tick, x, y, z). PURE."""
    (ta, xa), (tb, xb) = (a[0], a[1]), (b[0], b[1])
    if xa == xb:
        return float(ta)
    return ta + (tb - ta) * (x - xa) / (xb - xa)


def traverses(samples, tick_seconds):
    """Every crossing of a lane's stretch, either way, in samples
    [(tick, x, y, z)] in tick order: [{lane, seconds, peak, hops}]. A crossing
    starts where the bot enters the stretch from one end and counts when it
    leaves by the other without having left the lane or the stretch's far
    side; turning back, leaving the lane, or a gap in the samples of more than
    a second drops it. PURE: the self-test holds it."""
    lo, hi = STRETCH
    out = []
    open_ = None
    for i in range(1, len(samples)):
        a, b = samples[i - 1], samples[i]
        if (b[0] - a[0]) * tick_seconds > 1.0 or teleported(a, b, tick_seconds):
            open_ = None
            continue
        lane = lane_of(b[2])
        if open_ is not None:
            if lane != open_["lane"]:
                open_ = None
            else:
                height = b[3] - FLOOR_Z
                open_["peak"] = max(open_["peak"], height)
                if height > HOP_UNITS and not open_["up"]:
                    open_["hops"] += 1
                open_["up"] = height > HOP_UNITS
                exit_x = hi if open_["east"] else lo
                back_x = lo if open_["east"] else hi
                if (a[1] - exit_x) * (b[1] - exit_x) <= 0 and a[1] != b[1]:
                    seconds = (crossing_tick(a, b, exit_x) - open_["start"]) * tick_seconds
                    out.append({"lane": open_["lane"] + ("-east" if open_["east"] else "-west"), "seconds": seconds,
                                "peak": open_["peak"], "hops": open_["hops"]})
                    open_ = None
                    continue
                if (a[1] - back_x) * (b[1] - back_x) < 0:
                    open_ = None
        if open_ is None and lane is not None and lane == lane_of(a[2]) and a[1] != b[1]:
            for enter_x, east in ((lo, True), (hi, False)):
                moving = b[1] > a[1] if east else b[1] < a[1]
                if moving and (a[1] - enter_x) * (b[1] - enter_x) <= 0:
                    open_ = {"lane": lane, "east": east, "start": crossing_tick(a, b, enter_x), "peak": max(0.0, b[3] - FLOOR_Z),
                             "hops": 0, "up": b[3] - FLOOR_Z > HOP_UNITS}
    return out


def teleported(a, b, tick_seconds):
    """Whether the step from sample a to sample b is faster than anything a player does. PURE."""
    seconds = max((b[0] - a[0]) * tick_seconds, 1e-6)
    return ((b[1] - a[1]) ** 2 + (b[2] - a[2]) ** 2) ** 0.5 / seconds > TELEPORT_SPEED


def flight_units(jumps):
    """The rise that tells a flight from a hop: half the lowest apex of the plans in a read of /ai/jumps (the
    game's own rule, RocketJumpProgram.FlownShare), and FLIGHT_UNITS at the most or with no plans. PURE."""
    apexes = [p["apex"] for p in (jumps or {}).get("plans", []) if p.get("apex", 0) > 0]
    return min(FLIGHT_UNITS, 0.5 * min(apexes)) if apexes else FLIGHT_UNITS


def flights(samples, tick_seconds, units=FLIGHT_UNITS):
    """Every time off the floor that rose past units, in samples
    [(tick, x, y, z)]: [{air, along, walked, peak}], from the last sample on
    the floor to the first back on it. PURE."""
    out = []
    start = None
    peak = 0.0
    for i in range(1, len(samples)):
        a, b = samples[i - 1], samples[i]
        if teleported(a, b, tick_seconds):
            start = None
            continue
        up = b[3] - FLOOR_Z > 1.0
        if start is None:
            if up and a[3] - FLOOR_Z <= 1.0:
                start, peak = a, b[3] - FLOOR_Z
            continue
        peak = max(peak, b[3] - FLOOR_Z)
        if not up:
            if peak > units:
                air = (b[0] - start[0]) * tick_seconds
                along = ((b[1] - start[1]) ** 2 + (b[2] - start[2]) ** 2) ** 0.5
                out.append({"air": round(air, 2), "along": round(along, 1), "walked": round(air * WALK_SPEED, 1), "peak": round(peak, 1)})
            start = None
    return out


def summary(found):
    """Per lane and direction: n, the median seconds and speed, the highest peak, the mean hops. PURE."""
    out = {}
    for lane in [l + d for l in LANES for d in ("-east", "-west")]:
        mine = [t for t in found if t["lane"] == lane]
        if not mine:
            out[lane] = {"n": 0}
            continue
        seconds = statistics.median(t["seconds"] for t in mine)
        out[lane] = {"n": len(mine), "seconds": round(seconds, 2), "speed": round((STRETCH[1] - STRETCH[0]) / seconds, 1),
                     "peak": round(max(t["peak"] for t in mine), 1), "hops": round(sum(t["hops"] for t in mine) / len(mine), 2)}
    return out


def self_test():
    # The links mode's verdict on one try: by a link only when it got there and a link's jump landed near its touch.
    def lj(plan, end, off=1.0, felt=-1):
        return {"plan": plan, "end": end, "off_plan": off, "gap": 0.5, "felt_after_shot": felt}
    t = link_try([lj(LINK_ARGUMENT_BASE + 3, "Landed")], LEDGE_250, 100, 400)
    assert t["by_link"] and t["ticks"] == 300 and t["link_ids"] == [3] and t["gaps"] == [0.5], t
    assert not link_try([lj(LINK_ARGUMENT_BASE + 3, "Landed")], LEDGE_250, 100, None)["by_link"]
    assert not link_try([lj(7, "Landed")], LEDGE_250, 100, 400)["by_link"], "a stretch's jump is no link"
    far = link_try([lj(LINK_ARGUMENT_BASE + 3, "Landed", off=1400.0), lj(LINK_ARGUMENT_BASE + 3, "Landed")], LEDGE_250, 100, 400)
    assert far["ends"] == ["LandedElsewhere", "Landed"] and far["gaps"] == [0.5], far
    assert link_try([lj(LINK_ARGUMENT_BASE, "Fizzled", felt=1)], LEDGE_250, 0, None)["fizzled_felt_early"] == 1
    # A round's restart in mid-flight: the game ends the jump as Moved (lane G5e), which is no landing and no link's.
    moved = link_try([lj(LINK_ARGUMENT_BASE + 3, "Moved", off=1415.0), lj(LINK_ARGUMENT_BASE + 3, "Landed")], LEDGE_250, 100, 400)
    assert moved["ends"] == ["Moved", "Landed"] and moved["by_link"] and link_summary([moved])["first_jump_landed"] == 0, moved
    assert unpack_bin(4611688217487343636) == (20, 17, 0), unpack_bin(4611688217487343636)
    assert arrived((0, 1028.0, 1150.0, 266.0), LEDGE_250) and not arrived((0, 1028.0, 1150.0, 16.0), LEDGE_250)
    s = link_summary([far, t])
    assert (s["tries"], s["arrived"], s["by_link"], s["first_jump_landed"]) == (2, 2, 2, 1), s
    tick = 0.015
    # East along the run at 240 u/s, one sample every 7 ticks (25.2 u), flat.
    walk = [(i * 7, 300.0 + i * 25.2, 232.0, FLOOR_Z) for i in range(70)]
    got = traverses(walk, tick)
    assert len(got) == 1 and got[0]["lane"] == "run-east", got
    assert abs(got[0]["seconds"] - 1200.0 / 240.0) < 0.02, got
    assert got[0]["peak"] == 0 and got[0]["hops"] == 0, got
    # West along the low lane with one hop 60 u high in the middle.
    hop = [(i * 7, 1900.0 - i * 25.2, 632.0, FLOOR_Z + (60.0 if 30 <= i < 34 else 0.0)) for i in range(70)]
    got = traverses(hop, tick)
    assert len(got) == 1 and got[0]["lane"] == "low-west" and got[0]["hops"] == 1 and got[0]["peak"] == 60.0, got
    # Turning back before the far end is no traverse; nor is one that leaves the lane.
    back = walk[:30] + [(210 + i * 7, walk[29][1] - (i + 1) * 25.2, 232.0, FLOOR_Z) for i in range(40)]
    assert traverses(back, tick) == [], traverses(back, tick)
    out = [(t, x, 900.0 if 20 <= i < 24 else y, z) for i, (t, x, y, z) in enumerate(walk)]
    assert traverses(out, tick) == [], traverses(out, tick)
    # A gap in the samples of over a second drops the open traverse.
    gap = walk[:25] + [(t + 200, x, y, z) for (t, x, y, z) in walk[25:]]
    assert traverses(gap, tick) == [], traverses(gap, tick)
    # A restart puts the bot back on its spawn mid-traverse: no traverse, and the next one counts.
    restart = walk[:30] + [(210 + i * 7, 128.0 + i * 25.2, 136.0, FLOOR_Z) for i in range(80)]
    got = traverses(restart, tick)
    assert len(got) == 1 and abs(got[0]["seconds"] - 5.0) < 0.02, got
    assert traverses(walk[:30] + [(210, 128.0, 136.0, FLOOR_Z)], tick) == []
    # A flight: up 900 u over 3 s while drifting 150 u, then down; a 60 u hop is none.
    fly = [(i * 10, 300.0 + i * 7.5, 232.0, FLOOR_Z + (0.0 if i in (0, 21) else 900.0 - abs(i - 10.5) * 80.0)) for i in range(22)]
    got = flights(fly, tick)
    assert len(got) == 1 and abs(got[0]["air"] - 3.15) < 0.01 and abs(got[0]["along"] - 157.5) < 0.1 and got[0]["walked"] == 756.0, got
    assert flights(hop, tick) == [] and flights(walk, tick) == []
    # A flight that rises 150 u is one where the game's plans rise 240 (half of it is 120), and none against the 200 u of a game that serves no plans.
    low = [(i * 10, 300.0 + i * 30.0, 232.0, FLOOR_Z + (0.0 if i in (0, 11) else 150.0 - abs(i - 5.5) * 20.0)) for i in range(12)]
    assert flight_units({"plans": [{"apex": 240.0}, {"apex": 300.0}]}) == 120.0 and flight_units({"plans": [{"apex": 900.0}]}) == FLIGHT_UNITS
    assert flight_units(None) == FLIGHT_UNITS and flight_units({"plans": []}) == FLIGHT_UNITS
    assert flights(low, tick) == [] and len(flights(low, tick, 120.0)) == 1 and flights(hop, tick, 120.0) == []
    # Twice the speed is half the time: the stimulus reaches the number.
    fast = [(i * 7, 300.0 + i * 50.4, 232.0, FLOOR_Z) for i in range(40)]
    assert abs(traverses(fast, tick)[0]["seconds"] - 2.5) < 0.02
    # The jumps of an arm, from /ai/jumps before and after it: the counters' change, only the jumps the first read had not, one under the slab.
    def jump(serial, end, takeoff, touch, gap=None, launched=True, stood=0.0):
        return {"serial": serial, "end": end, "launched": launched, "takeoff": takeoff, "touch": touch, "air_seconds": 1.8, "plan_air_seconds": 1.785, "slid": 20.0,
                "approach_seconds": 1.0, "stood_seconds": stood, "rise": 210.0, "off_plan": 12.0, "plan_health": 28.7, "gap": gap}
    b = {"ai.jump.begun": 2, "ai.jump.landed.near": 1, "ai.jump.refused.ceiling": 1, "last": [jump(1, "Landed", [400, 232, 16], [1600, 232, 16], 5.0), jump(2, "ViewLate", [0, 0, 0], [0, 0, 0])]}
    e = {"ai.jump.begun": 6, "ai.jump.landed.near": 3, "ai.jump.refused.ceiling": 3, "ai.jump.refused.short": 2, "nav_sha256": "abc",
         "last": b["last"] + [jump(3, "Landed", [400, 232, 16], [1610, 232, 16], 8.0, stood=0.4), jump(4, "Landed", [1400, 632, 16], [900, 632, 16], 30.0, stood=0.6),
                              jump(5, "Astray", [1500, 632, 16], [1530, 632, 16], launched=False, stood=0.2), jump(6, "Landed", [400, 232, 16], [1590, 232, 16])]}
    got = jump_summary(b, e)
    # Of the three landed two stood, for 0.4 and 0.6 s; the one that did not land is listed with where it ended against its plan's takeoff.
    assert got["landed"]["stood_n"] == 2 and got["landed"]["stood"] == 0.5 and got["landed"]["rise"] == 210.0, got["landed"]
    assert got["off"] == [{"serial": 5, "end": "Astray", "after": 1.0, "stood": 0.2, "past": 30.0}], got["off"]
    assert got["counters"]["ai.jump.begun"] == 4 and got["counters"]["ai.jump.landed.near"] == 2 and got["counters"]["ai.jump.died"] == 0, got["counters"]
    assert got["refused"] == {"ceiling": 2, "short": 2} and got["ends"] == {"Landed": 3, "Astray": 1} and got["under_slab"] == 1, got
    assert got["landed"]["n"] == 3 and got["landed"]["ground"] == 1190.0 and got["landed"]["gap_n"] == 2 and got["landed"]["gap"] == 19.0 and got["landed"]["gap_worst"] == 30.0, got["landed"]
    assert jump_summary(None, None) is None and jump_summary(None, e)["counters"]["ai.jump.begun"] == 6
    assert under_slab([1000, 632, 16]) and not under_slab([400, 632, 16]) and not under_slab([1000, 232, 16])
    s = summary(traverses(walk, tick) + traverses(hop, tick))
